{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a7c91e22-f3b4-4d88-b012-8e5f3c7d9a01",
		"name": "Vigil Website",
		"description": "## Vigil Public Website — API Collection\n\nAll backend API calls used by the Vigil marketing/public website (`github.com/amandaptuar/vigil_website`).\n\n### Base URL\n`http://160-153-179-249.sslip.io`\n\n### Endpoints Covered\n| # | Endpoint | Auth | Used By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | GET /api/health | Public | Health check |\n| 2 | GET /api/subscriptions/plans | Public | Pricing page — fetch real plans |\n| 3a | POST /api/auth/register-website | Public | Register page — auto-generates username + temp password, emails credentials |\n| 3b | POST /api/auth/login | Public | Login with USERNAME + temp password, returns `must_reset_password: true` |\n| 3c | POST /api/auth/change-password-first-time | JWT | First-login mandatory password change |\n| 4 | POST /api/payments/checkout-session | Public | Pricing page — Stripe checkout |\n| 5 | POST /api/contact | Public | Contact page — contact form |\n\n### Registration Flow (Website)\n```\nUser fills Name + Email on website\n        ↓\nPOST /api/auth/register-website\n        ↓ backend auto-generates\n  username = \"john_a4b3\"\n  temp password = \"Vigil@8Xk3Mq2P\"\n  email sent to user (USERNAME + PASSWORD only — no email field)\n        ↓\nUser checks email → logs in with USERNAME + temp password\nPOST /api/auth/login → { must_reset_password: true }\n        ↓\nFrontend shows Change Password screen\nPOST /api/auth/change-password-first-time\n        ↓\nUser accesses full dashboard ✅\n```\n\n### CORS Note\nAdd the website production domain to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the VPS `.env` file.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "baseUrl",
			"value": "http://160-153-179-249.sslip.io",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Health Check",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
					"host": [
						"{{baseUrl}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"api",
						"health"
					]
				},
				"description": "Verify backend is online. Returns `{ status: 'ok', timestamp }`."
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('Backend is healthy', function () {",
							"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
							"  var json = pm.response.json();",
							"  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('ok');",
							"});"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Pricing — Get Subscription Plans",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/plans",
					"host": [
						"{{baseUrl}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"api",
						"subscriptions",
						"plans"
					]
				},
				"description": "Fetches all available subscription plans (Free, Basic, Premium, Family). Public endpoint — no auth required. The Pricing page uses this to show real plan names, prices, and features instead of hardcoded values."
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('Returns plans array', function () {",
							"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
							"  var json = pm.response.json();",
							"  // API returns { status, count, plans: [...] } — handle both shapes",
							"  var plans = Array.isArray(json) ? json : json.plans;",
							"  pm.expect(plans).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
							"});",
							"var json = pm.response.json();",
							"var plans = Array.isArray(json) ? json : (json.plans || []);",
							"if (plans.length > 0) {",
							"  pm.collectionVariables.set('planId', plans[0]._id || plans[0].id);",
							"  console.log('Captured planId:', pm.collectionVariables.get('planId'));",
							"}"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "3. Register & Login — Website Flow",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "3a. Register (Website — name + email + password)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register-website",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"register-website"
							]
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Parent\",\n  \"email\": \"website.test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Test@1234\",\n  \"mobile\": \"\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"description": "As of the July 2026 fix: the parent sets their OWN password on the form. No more auto-generated username/temp-password emailed to them. Returns a token immediately — redirect straight into Parent Web already signed in (see success handling in the website Register.jsx)."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"  var res = pm.response.json();",
									"  if (res.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", res.token); }",
									"  if (res.userId) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"parentId\", res.userId); }",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "3b. Login (email + password, set by the parent)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"website.test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Test@1234\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"description": "Same endpoint as before. must_reset_password will be false for anyone who registered after the fix — only legacy (pre-fix) accounts still get true."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"  var res = pm.response.json();",
									"  if (res.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", res.token); }",
									"  if (res.userId) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"parentId\", res.userId); }",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
